1
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:05,290
- Hey, can I ask you a question? - Sure.

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:06,740
You've had this dart board since I've known you,

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,150
but I've never seen you play.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:10,490
Oh, uh, we played... once.

5
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:12,340
I broke a window.

6
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:15,640
- What window? - That one over there.

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,910
Leonard, where are the Skee-Ball tickets?

8
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:19,970
Skee-Ball tickets?

9
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:22,430
Yeah, from when we went to the arcade three years ago?

10
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:25,110
I finally decided what prize I want.

11
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:27,910
Hurry up.

12
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:30,330
Uh, if I still have them,

13
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,340
they're probably in the junk box.

14
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,510
Ooh, what are you gonna get?

15
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:34,910
None of your business.

16
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:37,580
But when you see me wearing a flower

17
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:38,640
in my lapel later,

18
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,030
you are most welcome to sniff it.

19
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,490
Yup, oh... here you go.

20
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:45,680
Oh, thank you.

21
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:49,010
Here, get yourself an eraser for your troubles.

22
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:53,340
I forgot about this.

23
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:56,600
My aunt made it for me when I started college.

24
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:02,260
Aw, did she hate you?

25
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:04,990
Why? Because I got an ugly, itchy sweater,

26
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:07,640
and my brother got a car? No, I was her favorite.

27
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:10,390
Yeah, I seem to be a few tickets short.

28
00:01:10,390 --> 00:01:11,840
Are there more in the box?

29
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,800
Hmm, I think I got them all.

30
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:15,390
Nope, they're not in there.

31
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:17,630
Well, you barely looked. Let me see.

32
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:19,680
No, no, no, I-I looked, and...

33
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,250
No more tickets.

34
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,850
Leonard, let me look in the box.

35
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:24,240
Okay, okay!

36
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,270
I'm gonna show you what's in the box.

37
00:01:26,270 --> 00:01:29,380
but just... promise not to flip out.

38
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,910
Why would I flip out?

39
00:01:30,910 --> 00:01:32,230
Is it a spider?

40
00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:34,650
It's a spider!

41
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:37,140
No, if it was a spider,

42
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,130
Lenny would've flipped out.

43
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:40,720
Okay, Sheldon,

44
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:43,600
I know I was supposed to return this DVD a long time ago,

45
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,840
and I know we rented it on your card.

46
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,040
But it's been, like, seven years

47
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,470
and clearly nothing bad has happened.

48
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:51,490
So in-in-in-instead of being

49
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:54,110
a giant pain in the ass like you always are,

50
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:56,010
what if this one time

51
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:58,630
you just tried staying calm?

52
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:06,730
That seems like a reasonable request.

53
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:08,450
Although so did, "Hey, Leonard,

54
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:10,990
would you mind returning that DVD?"

55
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:14,850
I'm sorry. I'll-Ill take care of it.

56
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,490
Okay.

57
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,370
I mean it, I'm going to.

58
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,670
I believe you.

59
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:26,940
And you're going to stay calm?

60
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:28,990
I said I would.

61
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,320
How about that?

62
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:38,800
Sheldon's being reasonable.

63
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,510
Yeah, it's freaking me out. I'm gonna go.

64
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,240
So... when you say

65
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,770
you're not going to freak out about the DVD,

66
00:03:13,770 --> 00:03:16,200
here's what that means.

67
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:18,280
Don't fixate on it.

68
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,310
Don't wake me up in the middle of the night.

69
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:22,120
Or nag me through the door

70
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,060
while I'm on the toilet.

71
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,600
Okay, first, talking to you while you're on the toilet

72
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,920
isn't exactly a picnic for me either, okay?

73
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,330
Remember...

74
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:34,150
when you can hear me, I can hear you.

75
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:36,510
And second...

76
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:37,970
you completely disregard

77
00:03:37,970 --> 00:03:41,140
how uncomfortable unresolved issues are for me.

78
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:42,240
It's-it's like, a...

79
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:45,190
an itch in my brain I can't scratch.

80
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:46,440
When I broke my arm I used

81
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:48,820
to stick a coat hanger down there.

82
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:54,570
You ever try that? Maybe go in through the ear?

83
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:57,050
You wouldn't make jokes if you could feel the way I feel.

84
00:03:57,050 --> 00:03:59,230
Well, I don't know how to do that.

85
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,190
How about this?

86
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:05,580
I promise I won't pester you about the DVD.

87
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,860
You can defecate in peace.

88
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:11,050
That's a win for both of us. But...

89
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:13,820
until this matter is resolved,

90
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,500
I would like you

91
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,580
to wear this sweater.

92
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:22,410
With nothing underneath it.

93
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:26,010
That's stupid. Why?

94
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:28,550
You say it's itchy and uncomfortable.

95
00:04:28,550 --> 00:04:31,680
I say situations like this make me feel the same way.

96
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,260
I'm telling you, try the hanger.

97
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:37,000
Put it on.

98
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,260
Let's share the experience.

99
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,350
You got it.

100
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:43,700
If this sweater shuts you up,

101
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,710
I'm gonna make a fortune

102
00:04:44,710 --> 00:04:46,880
selling them to everyone we know.

103
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:49,450
Now...

104
00:04:49,450 --> 00:04:52,580
all I need to do is head down to the video store

105
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:55,660
and return the DVD.

106
00:04:58,910 --> 00:05:01,410
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

107
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:04,790
That store went out of business years ago.

108
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,460
Really?

109
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:13,140
How those nipples feeling, chief?

110
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,340
Penny, can we please get our drinks?

111
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,920
Yeah, hang on, just give me sec.

112
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:23,490
At work today, I did an in vivo stereotaxic surgery.

113
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:24,490
Cool. At my lab,

114
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:27,350
I performed ten laser capture micro-dissections.

115
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:30,070
I scraped gum off the bottom of that table.

116
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:33,340
Only 'cause my manager saw me put it there.

117
00:05:34,210 --> 00:05:35,480
Oh, my gosh.

118
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,650
That's the girl that broke Rajesh's heart.

119
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:38,790
That's Lucy?

120
00:05:38,790 --> 00:05:41,380
I don't know why but I always pictured her as Indian.

121
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:44,010
I think that reason's called racism.

122
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,570
I'm gonna go talk to her.

123
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:48,540
Why? What are you gonna say?

124
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:49,490
I'm not gonna say anything.

125
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:50,620
I just want to check her out.

126
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:51,650
Because she hurt my friend.

127
00:05:51,650 --> 00:05:54,280
My Indian friend.

128
00:05:54,870 --> 00:05:57,010
- Who's racist now? - You.

129
00:05:57,010 --> 00:06:00,360
Because you just called him your "Indian friend."

130
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:04,190
Yeah, well, you're short.

131
00:06:06,230 --> 00:06:07,970
We're never getting our drinks.

132
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,150
No, but we knew that.

133
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:13,160
Hey, can I start you off with something to drink?

134
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,660
- Oh, water would be great. - Okay.

135
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:17,790
Um, you're Lucy, right?

136
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:19,320
I'm a friend of Raj Koothrappali's.

137
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:21,340
Actually Amy recognized you.

138
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:30,810
How's he doing?

139
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:32,400
Oh, you know, he's good.

140
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,610
Great.

141
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,790
Yeah, this is none of my business.

142
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:39,430
But why did you break up with him in an e-mail?

143
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,020
Oh, I don't know.

144
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:43,360
I guess I thought it would be easier.

145
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:45,330
Yeah, I get that.

146
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:46,880
I'll go get you your water.

147
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,520
When you say "easier,"

148
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,490
you mean easier for you, right?

149
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:56,330
'Cause it certainly didn't make it easier for him.

150
00:06:56,330 --> 00:06:59,510
Any chance I can get a different waitress?

151
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,110
I-I'm sorry, this is rude of me.

152
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:02,940
I will go get that water.

153
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,390
See, see, see, see.

154
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:08,630
Just now you expressed your feelings to my face.

155
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,770
How come you could do that with me, but not Raj?

156
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:12,790
I don't know your e-mail.

157
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:15,230
You know what the worst part is?

158
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:16,800
You're sitting here, perfectly happy

159
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,820
and he's at home, a blubbering mess.

160
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,090
Oh, I thought you said he was okay.

161
00:07:20,090 --> 00:07:21,390
Well, I also said I was getting you water,

162
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:24,110
but look at me still standing here.

163
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,090
You know, I may be a bad waitress,

164
00:07:26,090 --> 00:07:27,980
but you are a bad person.

165
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:30,750
Now, you want to hear the specials?

166
00:07:51,030 --> 00:07:52,690
So, you can never take it off?

167
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,450
No.

168
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:55,820
Not even to sleep?

169
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:57,110
No.

170
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:59,190
So, you're just an idiot?

171
00:08:00,710 --> 00:08:02,710
It's called proving a point.

172
00:08:02,770 --> 00:08:04,490
Is the point you're an idiot?

173
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:07,240
Gentlemen, please.

174
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:11,320
Leonard is trying to walk a mile in my metaphorical shoes.

175
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,310
He can't walk in my actual shoes.

176
00:08:13,310 --> 00:08:15,400
He has the feet of a toddler.

177
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,870
So, how are you gonna return the DVD

178
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:20,270
if the store went out of business?

179
00:08:21,030 --> 00:08:22,580
Monday morning I'll go downtown

180
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,540
look up the owner's information.

181
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:27,370
And send him the DVD.

182
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,480
Pay the late fee.

183
00:08:32,190 --> 00:08:33,090
And prove to Sheldon

184
00:08:33,090 --> 00:08:35,050
that you can have a problem and solve it...

185
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:40,420
...without acting like a complete lunatic.

186
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:45,050
And the man impersonating a bear would like everyone to know

187
00:08:45,050 --> 00:08:47,840
that "Only you can prevent forest fires."

188
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:51,900
I don't get it.

189
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,180
- You didn't have Smokey the Bear in India? - No.

190
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:56,980
Oh, is he anything like, uh, Mun-Mun the Mongoose?

191
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,520
He taught us not to play with cobras.

192
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:05,140
You had to be taught not to play with cobras?

193
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:09,370
You had to be taught not to burn down the forest?

194
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:19,460
Hey, if you guys were hungry,

195
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:21,200
why didn't you order something at the restaurant?

196
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,980
We did, you never brought it.

197
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:27,100
Oh, that's right.

198
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,980
Nachos and a turkey club.

199
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,410
Not even close.

200
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:33,550
Well, I was too busy standing up

201
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:35,550
for my friend to worry about your...

202
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:38,600
I want to say salmon.

203
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,150
You want to say sorry.

204
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,830
So, how are you gonna tell Raj abut what you did?

205
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:50,450
What do you mean "how"? What's the big deal?

206
00:09:50,450 --> 00:09:52,660
You told Lucy he was a pathetic mess.

207
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:54,730
Then you made her cry and leave.

208
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:56,420
Okay, you guys are overreacting.

209
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:59,020
Raj is gonna appreciate how I had his back.

210
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,380
What is wrong with you, Penny?!

211
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:04,800
You ruined any chance I had of getting back with Lucy!

212
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,010
Now she knows I'm a desperate mess

213
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:09,460
instead of just being pretty sure!

214
00:10:11,930 --> 00:10:13,190
It's Lucy.

215
00:10:13,190 --> 00:10:14,960
She wants to meet for coffee.

216
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,340
I love you, Penny!

217
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:24,560
Hey, what're you working on?

218
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,330
I'm thinking about how one could use

219
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:29,880
the fact that a rapidly rotating mirror

220
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,160
turns virtual photons into real ones

221
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:35,120
as a method of observing dark energy.

222
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:37,150
That's a pretty cool idea.

223
00:10:37,150 --> 00:10:38,640
Yeah. It's great you're here.

224
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,590
I'd love to get an engineer's opinion.

225
00:10:40,590 --> 00:10:41,670
Sure.

226
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:43,930
This chair is squeaky.

227
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:50,200
Now, do I fix it or get a new one?

228
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:53,880
Well, Sheldon, it took me all morning,

229
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,450
but I found the owner of the video store.

230
00:10:56,450 --> 00:10:59,090
And I am happy to report that he died peacefully in his sleep,

231
00:10:59,090 --> 00:11:00,970
drunk at the bottom of a pool.

232
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,690
Anyway, there is no one to return the DVD to,

233
00:11:05,690 --> 00:11:09,380
so this issue is resolved.

234
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:13,700
And I'd just like to point out that

235
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:15,530
even though the sweater was uncomfortable,

236
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:17,510
I didn't use it as an excuse

237
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:20,100
to antagonize everyone around me.

238
00:11:20,270 --> 00:11:23,250
You know, you could reimburse the video store owner's next of kin.

239
00:11:23,250 --> 00:11:25,280
Or it's resolved!

240
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:30,170
Hey, that next of kin thing sounds pretty good.

241
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:34,030
I believe this is yours.

242
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:41,560
Can I ask you guys a question?

243
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,470
So, I'm seeing Lucy tomorrow night,

244
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:45,530
and I've never hung out with someone who broke up with me.

245
00:11:45,530 --> 00:11:46,810
How do you do it?

246
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:48,140
You can't let her know you're hurting.

247
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:49,750
You know, the key is confidence.

248
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,840
Why is the key always confidence?

249
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:55,380
How come it's never love handles and flop sweat?

250
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,870
If this girl hurt you so much,

251
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:00,540
are you sure you want to see her again?

252
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:01,610
Well, if I may...

253
00:12:01,610 --> 00:12:03,050
he has so little self-respect

254
00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:05,720
and is so desperate for the smallest crumb of affection,

255
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,540
she could literally sleep with his own father

256
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:09,530
in his own bed and post the video to YouTube,

257
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:11,280
and he'd still buy her flowers

258
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,950
and ask her to be his bride.

259
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,650
He's right.

260
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,050
But in my defense, if we could survive that,

261
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:24,200
we could survive anything.

262
00:12:25,630 --> 00:12:26,940
Well, if you're sure you want to do this,

263
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:27,940
it's only coffee...

264
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:30,280
just relax and see what happens.

265
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:33,250
- Well, can I say she looks nice? - Sure.

266
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,000
Can I tell her I miss her?

267
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,780
Maybe, if she asks.

268
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:38,180
Oh, can I show her an oil painting I made

269
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:41,120
of us surrounded by our children and grandchildren?

270
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:45,970
I'd save that for the second date.

271
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:47,530
Good, good.

272
00:12:47,530 --> 00:12:49,070
'Cause no matter how hard I try,

273
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:51,800
I cannot get the twins to look alike.

274
00:12:58,370 --> 00:12:59,350
What are you doing?

275
00:12:59,350 --> 00:13:02,190
Oh, I'm just trying to find the stupid next of kin

276
00:13:02,190 --> 00:13:05,540
to this stupid video store owner so I can return the DVD

277
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,460
and see the look on Sheldon's stupid face

278
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:11,290
when he sees that I didn't let this get to me.

279
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,070
Sheldon's not here.

280
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:15,390
Why don't you take the sweater off?

281
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:17,550
Th-Th-There's a principle at stake!

282
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:19,010
- Which is? - Oh, I don't know.

283
00:13:19,010 --> 00:13:20,850
Who cares? Look at me!

284
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,510
Oh, my God!

285
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,780
Is that sweater made of bees?

286
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:27,410
Come on, take it off. I won't tell.

287
00:13:27,410 --> 00:13:29,570
No, no, honey, if I take it off, Sheldon wins.

288
00:13:29,570 --> 00:13:30,470
Sweetie...

289
00:13:30,470 --> 00:13:32,830
every night you don't kill him in his sleep,

290
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:34,520
he wins.

291
00:13:35,830 --> 00:13:37,810
Nah, I-it's... it's almost done.

292
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:40,130
I just, I have to find...the next of kin,

293
00:13:40,130 --> 00:13:41,370
and send 'em the DVD

294
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:43,590
and then just wait for someone with my complexion to die

295
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:45,580
so I can get a skin graft.

296
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:48,720
Smile.

297
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:50,300
What-what is that? What is that for?

298
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,410
So you can send it to Princeton

299
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:53,280
and get your money back.

300
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,070
I must say, Sheldon,

301
00:13:59,070 --> 00:14:00,580
you're handling this DVD business

302
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,610
with an impressive amount of maturity.

303
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:04,710
I don't know why that surprises you.

304
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:06,130
I'm a grown man.

305
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:08,220
As should be evident by this sport coat

306
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:11,180
and very real flower in my lapel.

307
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,110
Is there some kind of new coping mechanism you're employing?

308
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:18,160
The more interesting question you should be asking is,

309
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:21,030
"What does this flower smell like?"

310
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,670
I'm gonna go with sad.

311
00:14:25,930 --> 00:14:28,120
So what's the story with you and this DVD?

312
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,600
There's nothing to tell.

313
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,510
Maybe I purchased a book entitled,

314
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:33,330
Don't Sweat the Small Stuff

315
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,940
and I followed its wise suggestions,

316
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:37,240
one of which was:

317
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:39,800
stop and smell the flowers.

318
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:43,720
- Seriously? - Please.

319
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:01,700
- Hi. - Hello.

320
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:04,010
Oh, it's so good to see you.

321
00:15:04,010 --> 00:15:05,350
You, too.

322
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:06,720
Please, sit.

323
00:15:07,190 --> 00:15:08,600
I, uh, I got you a cappuccino.

324
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,270
I remembered it was your favorite.

325
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:11,530
I also got crumb cake,

326
00:15:11,530 --> 00:15:14,250
but I remembered it was my favorite and I ate it.

327
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:18,230
Anyway, uh, how are you?

328
00:15:18,230 --> 00:15:20,080
I'm pretty good.

329
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:22,350
Listen, I just wanted to apologize

330
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:24,190
for breaking up with you in an e-mail.

331
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:25,260
Well, and I ate all the crumb cake.

332
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,800
we both made mistakes.

333
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,360
Okay.

334
00:15:29,850 --> 00:15:31,350
I'm so happy you asked me here,

335
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:33,930
and I hope we can hang out again sometime.

336
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,580
You know, as friends,

337
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:37,260
lovemaking partners, whatever.

338
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:43,650
I'm kind of seeing someone.

339
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,820
I think I know the answer to this,

340
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,650
but just to be clear, it's not me, right?

341
00:15:51,370 --> 00:15:53,270
This is all your fault!

342
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:55,420
I should've listened to Mun-Mun

343
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,010
because I've been playing with a cobra

344
00:15:57,010 --> 00:15:59,040
and her name is Penny!

345
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:00,820
Why are you so cruel?

346
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:02,240
Do you enjoy my pain?

347
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,340
There's a girl at the Cheesecake Factory I can set you up with.

348
00:16:04,810 --> 00:16:06,730
I love you, Penny!

349
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,400
How is it I can conceptualize a methodology

350
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,610
of examining dark matter in the universe

351
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:17,890
but can't figure out how to fix a novelty squirt flower?

352
00:16:19,410 --> 00:16:20,470
I think the real question is,

353
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:24,150
why do you waste your time with cheap, childish pranks?

354
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,260
There's probably a deep reason.

355
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:28,330
Which I'd be happy to discuss with you

356
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:31,060
over some peanut brittle in a can.

357
00:16:32,230 --> 00:16:34,790
Okay, Sheldon, I am out of options!

358
00:16:34,790 --> 00:16:37,440
Video store owner, Nursis Manookian,

359
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,360
has no next of kin!

360
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,000
Well, you seem hot under the collar...

361
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,110
or is that the sweater?

362
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,410
Oh, oh, no, no.

363
00:16:45,410 --> 00:16:47,500
I-It's because I spent all afternoon

364
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,160
at the Armenian church where his funeral mass was held.

365
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,930
According to Father Solakian,

366
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:53,440
no one attended.

367
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,430
Luckily, my trip wasn't a complete waste.

368
00:16:55,430 --> 00:16:56,990
I lit a candle and prayed for your death.

369
00:16:56,990 --> 00:16:59,620
But I'm not Armenian, so it probably won't work!

370
00:17:01,730 --> 00:17:03,590
This is over, right?

371
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:05,600
Oh, not necessarily.

372
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:09,180
I suggest you look for long-lost relatives

373
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:12,680
either in Armenia or Lebanon.

374
00:17:14,230 --> 00:17:15,880
Listen to me, Sheldon.

375
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,910
I am not going to Lebanon

376
00:17:17,910 --> 00:17:21,770
to return Super Mario Bros. the movie!

377
00:17:23,370 --> 00:17:25,170
You know, it might be fun.

378
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:27,490
You love hummus.

379
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:30,720
Why isn't this bothering you?

380
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,950
I-Isn't your brain getting itchy?

381
00:17:32,950 --> 00:17:35,330
This is on your card.

382
00:17:35,330 --> 00:17:37,490
This could be ruining your credit score!

383
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:41,070
Why isn't this making you crazy?

384
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,720
Leonard...

385
00:17:45,350 --> 00:17:47,230
I have something to tell you,

386
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:50,330
but I want you to promise not to flip out.

387
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:52,060
What?

388
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,190
Seven years ago,

389
00:17:55,190 --> 00:17:57,360
I found out the DVD was late

390
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,330
and I paid for it.

391
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:08,170
What?

392
00:18:09,370 --> 00:18:11,190
I was going to mention it at the time,

393
00:18:11,190 --> 00:18:13,800
but then I thought, some day,

394
00:18:14,710 --> 00:18:17,460
this might be a teachable moment.

395
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:42,350
I... You...

396
00:18:42,350 --> 00:18:43,410
How can...

397
00:18:43,870 --> 00:18:45,570
What?!

398
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:51,580
Sheldon...

399
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:53,870
that was diabolical.

400
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,680
I know.

401
00:18:57,190 --> 00:18:58,450
And it wasn't easy.

402
00:18:58,450 --> 00:19:01,680
Do you have any idea what it's like to wait for years

403
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:04,720
and never know if you're going to finally get satisfaction?

404
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:15,520
You're even prettier than Penny said.

405
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,930
I can't believe a girl like you

406
00:19:16,930 --> 00:19:18,300
doesn't have a boyfriend.

407
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,230
Well, I don't.

408
00:19:19,230 --> 00:19:21,440
I don't believe you, you're lying to me!

409
00:19:22,610 --> 00:19:23,650
What?

410
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:24,580
Oh, it's okay.

411
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,560
I have no morals and I'm desperately lonely.

412
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:27,380
I'll be the other man

413
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:30,060
if you want a little something-something on the side.

414
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:32,480
What is wrong with you?!

415
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,180
What is wrong with you?!

416
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:36,250
What is wrong with you?!

